  "summary": "Across 45 job postings from January 2025 to June 2026, the Saudi market shows a decisive shift toward data, AI, and cloud-native skills: SQL, Python, Machine Learning, Kubernetes, and Cloud Computing are all growing strongly, and six skills — including Generative AI, Azure, Terraform, TypeScript, Node.js, and Data Visualization — appear exclusively in the most recent period as sharp emerging signals. Traditional infrastructure (Networking, Linux) and generic productivity skills (Excel, Communication) are declining as explicit requirements. Education providers should prioritise full-stack data engineering pipelines, cloud-multi-platform literacy, and applied AI modules within the next curriculum cycle. Caution is warranted: with only 45 source postings, growth rates are directionally informative but statistically fragile, and all forecasts should be revisited when a larger dataset is available.",
